Replace the legacy logic with a Stable-POC Mean Reversion + Liquidity-Floor FVG Mitigation module. Preserve the 09:30 UTC opening buffer. Block trades when the anchored session POC has drifted more than 0.05 ATR over 6 bars. Block trades when current tick volume is below 80% of its 20-bar average. Block trades when ADX > 20 to avoid fading trending regimes. Enter only when price is extended between 1.5 and 3.0 ATR from the stable POC, a fresh FVG (≤6 bars) sits between the POC and the extended price, and the current bar closes back through VWAP in the fade direction. Short fade: close < open and close < session VWAP. Long fade: close > open and close > session VWAP.

Exact MQL5 logic:

input int    SESSION_START_HOUR   = 9;
input int    SESSION_START_MIN    = 30;
input int    OPENING_BUFFER_MIN   = 5;
input int    NO_NEW_ENTRY_HOUR    = 11;
input int    NO_NEW_ENTRY_MIN     = 30;
input double MIN_ATR              = 12.0;
input double MAX_ADX              = 20.0;
input double POC_STABILITY_ATR    = 0.05;
