New self-healing logic for Module_1_DE40_VPPOC:
- Enforce 09:30 UTC session start + 5-minute opening buffer (validated fix).
- No new entries after 10:30 UTC to avoid the 11:00 off-hours illiquidity cluster; open positions can still be managed until 11:30 UTC.
- Use current 5-minute volume > 1.25 * 20-bar average volume to avoid 10:00 off-hours illiquidity.
- Use ADX < 20.0 as a regime gate. This directly blocks the old losing Regime_1_Bull_Trend with ADX 22, unlike OLS R²/slope thresholds that were not restrictive enough.
- Compute developing session POC and VWAP. Use anchor = POC if |POC - VWAP| / ATR < 0.25, otherwise use VWAP as dynamic fair value.
- Do NOT use the old 2.0 ATR extension requirement, old session high/low sweep, old FVG-at-POC overlap, or old OBV/MFI absorption logic.
- Long entry requires a false breakdown: Low[0] < anchor, Close[0] > anchor, Close[0] > Open[0], plus a fresh bullish FVG formed within the last 3 bars whose midpoint is below the anchor, and current price is inside a low-volume node (volume intensity < 0.50 relative to POC).
- Short entry requires a false breakout: High[0] > anchor, Close[0] < anchor, Close[0] < Open[0], plus a fresh bearish FVG formed within the last 3 bars whose midpoint is above the anchor, and current price is inside a low-volume node.
- DXY macro gate: block longs when DXY beta < -0.75 and DXY momentum > 0; block shorts when DXY beta < -0.75 and DXY momentum < 0.

Exact MQL5 reference logic:

#include <Trade\Trade.mqh>
CTrade trade;

input int    SESSION_START_HOUR   = 9;
input int    SESSION_START_MIN    = 30;
input int    BUFFER_MINUTES       = 5;
